Package: dmrseqx
Type: Package
Title: Fast Detection of Differentially Methylated Regions Following dmrseq
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jiantao", "Shi", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "jtshi@cmpt.ac.cn"),
    person("Keegan", "Korthauer", role = "cph",
           comment = "author of dmrseq, from which parts of the R code are adapted"))
Description: Detects differentially methylated regions from bisulfite sequencing
    counts with the procedure of 'dmrseq' (Korthauer et al. 2019,
    <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/kxy007>): candidate regions from smoothed
    differences, a region level generalized least squares model with correlated
    errors, and a pooled permutation null. All steps are written in C and run in
    threads, so that a whole genome takes minutes. It compares two or more groups
    or follows a continuous covariate. It is an independent reimplementation and
    is not affiliated with the authors of 'dmrseq'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    bsseq,
    GenomicRanges,
    IRanges,
    matrixStats (>= 1.0.0),
    methods,
    S4Vectors,
